          <attvalue for="0" value="action" />
          <attvalue for="3" value="1" />
          <attvalue for="5" value="# Task: Find a workout class for this upcoming Saturday in San Francisco&#10;&#10;I need to search for workout classes in San Francisco that are happening this upcoming Saturday. I'll approach this systematically by searching for relevant information and visiting websites to find specific classes.&#10;&#10;Thought: First, I need to determine the date of the upcoming Saturday to make my search more precise. Then I'll search for workout classes in San Francisco specifically for that date.&#10;&#10;Code:&#10;```py&#10;import datetime&#10;&#10;# Get today's date&#10;today = datetime.datetime.now()&#10;&#10;# Calculate days until next Saturday (where Monday is 0 and Sunday is 6)&#10;days_until_saturday = (5 - today.weekday()) % 7&#10;if days_until_saturday == 0:  # If today is Saturday, get next Saturday&#10;    days_until_saturday = 7&#10;&#10;# Calculate the date of the upcoming Saturday&#10;next_saturday = today + datetime.timedelta(days=days_until_saturday)&#10;next_saturday_formatted = next_saturday.strftime(&quot;%B %d, %Y&quot;)&#10;&#10;print(f&quot;Today is: {today.strftime('%A, %B %d, %Y')}&quot;)&#10;print(f&quot;Upcoming Saturday is: {next_saturday_formatted}&quot;)&#10;```&lt;end_code&gt;" />
          <attvalue for="6" value="Execution logs:&#10;Today is: Monday, April 28, 2025&#10;Upcoming Saturday is: May 03, 2025&#10;Last output from code snippet:&#10;None" />
