          <attvalue for="5" value="Thought: Based on my research, I've found several promising workout classes available in San Francisco on Saturdays. While I couldn't find specific classes for May 3, 2025 (as most studios don't schedule that far in advance), I've identified three excellent options that regularly offer Saturday classes and have good reviews:&#10;&#10;1. Barry's Bootcamp: They have multiple locations in San Francisco (Castro, Marina, FiDi) with Saturday classes typically running from morning to afternoon. Their Castro location is particularly popular, offering high-intensity interval training combining treadmill and strength training.&#10;&#10;2. BODYROK: Offers 45-minute pilates-inspired, full-body strength training classes on their custom reformers. They have multiple locations including Marina, FiDi, and Polk Street. Saturday classes are typically available mornings until early afternoon.&#10;&#10;3. HIT Fit SF: Specializes in boxing and HIIT classes, with 60-minute full-body workouts. They're known for their inclusive environment and flexible class options, including their signature &quot;HIIT Fit&quot; and &quot;Quickies&quot; (40-minute condensed versions of their workouts).&#10;&#10;Let me check the direct websites of these studios to see what additional information I can find:&#10;&#10;Code:&#10;```py&#10;# Let's try to visit their direct websites to get more information&#10;studio_urls = [&#10;    &quot;https://www.barrys.com/studio/castro/&quot;,&#10;    &quot;https://bodyrok.com/&quot;,&#10;    &quot;https://www.hitfitsf.com/&quot;&#10;]&#10;&#10;for url in studio_urls:&#10;    print(f&quot;\n--- Checking {url} ---&quot;)&#10;    try:&#10;        content = visit_webpage(url=url)&#10;        print(content[:1000])  # Print just the beginning to check&#10;    except Exception as e:&#10;        print(f&quot;Error accessing {url}: {e}&quot;)&#10;```&lt;end_code&gt;" />
