          <attvalue for="5" value="Thought: Based on all my research, I now have enough information to provide some good recommendations for workout classes in San Francisco on Saturday, May 3, 2025. While specific schedules for that exact date aren't available yet (as it's more than a year away), I can recommend several highly-rated studios that regularly offer Saturday classes.&#10;&#10;Let me summarize the best options:&#10;&#10;Code:&#10;```py&#10;final_answer(&quot;&quot;&quot;&#10;Here are some excellent workout class options for Saturday, May 3, 2025 in San Francisco:&#10;&#10;1. **Barry's Bootcamp**&#10;   - Multiple locations: Castro, Marina, and FiDi&#10;   - Known for high-intensity interval training combining treadmill and strength training&#10;   - Saturday hours: Typically 7:00 AM - 4:00 PM&#10;   - Classes are 50-60 minutes&#10;   - Very popular, so booking in advance is recommended&#10;   - Website: https://www.barrys.com/studio/castro/&#10;&#10;2. **BODYROK**&#10;   - Locations: Marina, FiDi, Polk Street&#10;   - Offers 45-minute Pilates-inspired full-body strength training&#10;   - Uses custom reformers for a unique workout experience&#10;   - Saturday classes typically run mornings until early afternoon&#10;   - Great for all fitness levels&#10;   - Website: https://bodyrok.com/&#10;&#10;3. **HIT Fit SF**&#10;   - Offers both boxing and HIIT classes&#10;   - 60-minute full-body workouts and 40-minute &quot;Quickies&quot; for those short on time&#10;   - Known for their inclusive environment&#10;   - Flexible membership options including drop-ins&#10;   - Website: https://www.hitfitsf.com/&#10;&#10;Since your chosen date is more than a year away, exact schedules aren't posted yet. I recommend checking their websites or using ClassPass closer to the date to book your preferred class. All these studios have excellent reviews and regularly offer Saturday morning and afternoon classes.&#10;&quot;&quot;&quot;)&#10;```&lt;end_code&gt;" />
